cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, empirical falsification dataset, SAT witness suite, or Lean 4 formal proof corpus in your research, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "Phase-SHA: A 14-Paradigm Reproducible Empirical & Formal Cryptanalysis Benchmark for SHA-256 and Bitcoin Double-SHA256"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-26"
license: MIT
authors:
  - alias: "CheeseGhostfox"
    email: "cheese_ghostfox2025@outlook.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/CheeseGhostfox/Phase-SHA-Cryptanalysis-Benchmark"
abstract: >-
  Phase-SHA (V1-V12) is an open, fully reproducible empirical and formal cryptanalysis
  benchmark evaluating 14 distinct paradigms (V11 P1-P11 and V12 P12, P13, P15) on
  reduced-round and full SHA-256 and Bitcoin Double-SHA256. It combines strict pure
  IEEE-754 FP32 GPU experiments (allow_tf32=False), isomorphic spectrum-aligned random
  control ciphers, 50/50 bit-exact SAT message-pair witnesses, gate-equivalent hardware
  amortization bounds, automated OR-Tools/Z3 Meet-in-the-Middle and Biclique bounds,
  and 32 Lean 4.36.0 source files containing 483 machine-checked theorem/lemma
  declarations (338 public + 145 private/protected) with zero sorry statements.
keywords:
  - SHA-256
  - Double-SHA256
  - Bitcoin mining
  - AsicBoost
  - Meet-in-the-Middle
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - SAT cryptanalysis
  - tensor networks
  - negative results
  - reproducible benchmark
